**`server.js`**
```js
const express = require('express');

const app = express();
const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;

app.get('/time', (req, res) => {
  const now = new Date();
  res.json({
    iso: now.toISOString(),
    unix: Math.floor(now.getTime() / 1000),
    timezone: Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone,
    local: now.toString(),
  });
});

app.listen(PORT, () => {
  console.log(`Time server listening on http://localhost:${PORT}/time`);
});
```

**`package.json`**
```json
{
  "name": "time-server",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "main": "server.js",
  "scripts": { "start": "node server.js" },
  "dependencies": { "express": "^4.19.2" }
}
```

To run it:
```bash
npm install
npm start
curl http://localhost:3000/time
```

`GET /time` returns JSON with the current time as an ISO string, a Unix timestamp, the server's timezone and the local time string. The port defaults to 3000 and can be changed with the `PORT` environment variable.

